The '''2024–25 season''' was the 118th season in the history of '''[[Sevilla FC|Sevilla Fútbol Club]]''', and the club's 24th consecutive season in [[La Liga]]. In addition to the [[2024–25 La Liga|domestic league]], the club participated in the [[2024–25 Copa del Rey|Copa del Rey]].

== Summary ==
On 2 June 2024, Sevilla announced the signing of [[García Pimienta]], who left [[UD Las Palmas|Las Palmas]], on a two-season contract.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://sevillafc.es/en/actual/news/francisco-javier-garcia-pimienta-new-coach|title=García Pimienta appointed as new Head Coach|publisher=Sevilla FC|date=2 June 2024}}</ref> On 12 July, the Andalusian club signed a contract with Arsenal's Belgian player [[Albert Sambi Lokonga]], with the right to purchase included.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://lastwordonsports.com/football/2024/07/13/arsenal-albert-lokonga-sevilla-loan-agreement/|title='Signed All Documents': Arsenal Poised To Offload Midfielder - Buy Option and Sell-On Clause Included|first=Uttiyo|last=Sarkar|date=13 July 2024}}</ref> On 15 July, Sevilla reached an agreement to bring [[Atletico Madrid]] midfielder [[Saúl (footballer, born 1994)|Saúl]] on loan.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.besoccer.com/new/official-saul-niguez-joins-sevilla-on-loan-from-atletico-madrid-1323558|title=OFFICIAL: Saul Niguez joins Sevilla on loan from Atletico Madrid|website=Besoccer|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240717055654/https://www.besoccer.com/new/official-saul-niguez-joins-sevilla-on-loan-from-atletico-madrid-1323558|archive-date=17 July 2024|access-date=17 July 2024|url-status=dead}}</ref>

On 31 July, it was announced that Nigerian striker [[Kelechi Iheanacho]] had signed on a free transfer.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://onefootball.com/en/news/kelechi-iheanacho-joins-sevilla-on-a-free-transfer-39833895|title=Kelechi Iheanacho joins Sevilla on a free transfer|date=2 September 2024|website=OneFootball}}</ref> On 2 September, [[Loïc Badé]] extended his contract until 2029.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.diariodesevilla.es/sevillafc/oficial-loic-bade-sevillista-2029_0_2002328454.html|title=Oficial: Loïc Badé, sevillista hasta 2029|first=Mario|last=Míjenz|date=2 September 2024|website=Diario de Sevilla|language=es}}</ref> On 24 September, Pimienta extended his contract for a third season.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.besoccer.com/new/official-sevilla-renew-pimienta-until-2027-after-valladolid-win-1331895|title=OFFICIAL: Sevilla renew Pimienta until 2027 after Valladolid win|website=www.besoccer.com}}</ref>

